<title>USA: MBIA qualifies seven issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies seven issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp. said it has qualified for bond insurance the following seven municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Bridgewater, Mass., $5 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--South Hadley, Mass., $2.025 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Holland, Mich., $11 million water supply system revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--Willmar, Minn., $1.265 million GO improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Binghamton City CD, N.Y., $2.75 million school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Pulaski CSD, N.Y., $3.327 million school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Suffern, N.Y., $1.935 million various purpose bonds.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
</text>
